Cube 2: Hypercube (stylized on-screen as Cube²: Hypercube) is a 2002 Canadian science fiction horror film directed by
Andrzej Sekuła, written by Sean Hood, and produced by Ernie Barbarash, Peter Block, and Suzanne Colvin.

11
01:00:49,411 --> 01:00:55,411
It is the second installment in the Cube film
series and a sequel to Cube (1997).

12
01:06:21,176 --> 01:06:27,176
Released in 2002, Hypercube replaces the colored industrial-style rooms
of the first film with high-tech, brightly lit chambers.

13
01:11:52,941 --> 01:11:58,941
Instead of industrial traps such as flamethrowers and extending spikes, the rooms
have "evolved" to control illusions, time, space, and reality.

14
01:17:24,705 --> 01:17:30,705
The film's critical reception was mixed, with reviewers panning the sequel's poorly produced CGI, writing,
and production, but praising its evolution from the first film, its acting, and its suspense.

15
01:22:56,470 --> 01:23:02,470
The film explores themes of hacker, riddle,
detective, mathematics, claustrophobia.

16
01:28:28,235 --> 01:28:34,235
The tone is mind_bending and thought_provoking and intense.
